       "content": "# Solving $(26^2 - 24^2 - 10)^2 - 10^2$\n\n## Step 1: Compute $26^2 - 24^2$\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n$$26^2 - 24^2 = (26-24)(26+24) = 2 \\times 50 = 100$$\n\n## Step 2: Subtract 10\n\n$$26^2 - 24^2 - 10 = 100 - 10 = 90$$\n\n## Step 3: Square the result and subtract $10^2$\n\n$$90^2 - 10^2 = 8100 - 100 = 8000$$\n\n## Final Answer\n\n$$\\boxed{8000}$$",
